{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310526,"nonce":"kZNGhZ7/2+OXPxM99b9netREwHI=","title":"FIXED 2026-06-12 (commit 60bbbf2). AOT llama-chat SIGSEGV at first interface dispatch — three stacked causes. llama-chat AOT now streams ...","message":"**Fixed at commit 60bbbf2 (2026-06-12).** AOT-compiled llama-chat crashed\nat `model.resetCache()` (first interface dispatch). Three stacked causes,\neach masking the next:\n\n1. **cmd_aot manifest gap.** Explicit-file invocations never loaded\n   rayzor.toml → no class-paths, no native-libs plugin. Cross-file\n   resolution then silently degraded: elision (rest of caller DCE'd) or\n   bare-name near-match (`Loader.load` → `SIMD4f_load`,\n   `KVCache.append` → bare `_append` extern that failed at link;\n   `free`/`alloc` would bind to LIBC silently). Fixed by\n   find_project_root from entry file dir + un-swallowing native-lib\n   load errors.\n\n2. **find_startup_llvm_names dropped 33 of 35 `__vtable_init__` hooks**\n   (func_id→symbol mapping was brittle). Runtime iface-vtable registry\n   ended up with 1 entry → `haxe_iface_fat_ptr_build` returned null →\n   dispatch on null fat ptr. Fixed by scanning LLVM module directly for\n   defined `__vtable_init__*`/`__init__*` (vtable regs ordered before\n   user inits).\n\n3. **Thunk name collision (the subtle one).** `ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk`\n   named thunks `__vtable_dispatch_thunk_{LOCAL_func_id}` — local ids\n   collide across modules post-merge, LLVM dedup-renames duplicates, and\n   slot FunctionRefs that escaped renumbering bound to the FIRST module's\n   same-named thunk. CLM slot 2 (forwardIds) held a foreign thunk\n   forwarding into an unrelated `forward(x:Tensor)` → x.shape() on a\n   token Array → EXC_BAD_ACCESS 0xb in rayzor_tensor_shape. Fixed:\n   thunks named by sanitized QUALIFIED method name.\n\n**Debugging leverage for next time:** `RAYZOR_IFACE_DEBUG=1` (kept,\nenv-gated) — `haxe_iface_vtable_set_slot` logs (class, iface, slot) with\ndladdr-symbolized inner fn ptr; fat_ptr_build logs null/miss + registry\nsize; hir_to_mir logs vtable emission method order at compile. The\nslot-symbolization is what cracked cause 3 — slots 0/3 had\nrenumber-suffixed thunk names, slots 1/2 unsuffixed (raw-id) ones.\n\n**Diagnosis shortcuts that worked:** [aot.gen]/[aot.reset] probes\nlocalized dispatch-vs-body; `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` diff between\n`rayzor run` and `rayzor aot` MIR exposed the divergence; `nm` +\n`objdump --disassemble-symbols=_main` counted init calls (4 vs 35).\n\n**Still open (separate bugs):**\n- Interface method call DIRECTLY off an anon-struct field (no\n  intervening cast) fails on BOTH JIT (silent skip) and AOT (devirt +\n  raw slot value as receiver → crash). llama-chat avoids via explicit\n  `cast(loaded.model, CausalLanguageModel)`. Repro: /tmp/aot_iface_repro3\n  Main4.hx.\n- No-rayzor.toml cross-file compile still silently breaks ([[feedback_no_silent_dispatch_fallthrough]]\n  violations): DYNAMIC-STDLIB bare-name fallback needs a hard-error\n  guard when the receiver class is statically known; unresolved\n  user-method CallDirect should be a compile error, not elision.\n- AOT decode 62.8 tok/s vs ~72 JIT server — gap unexplored (probe\n  traces, opt levels, single run; no tuning attempted).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_aot_iface_dispatch_fixed` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}